# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), names Cure Beast to Dying of the Light. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Cure Beast": ["A beast you can see within range regains hit points equal to 1d6 + your spellcasting modifier.",
 "A beast you can see within range regains hit points equal to 1d6 + your spellcasting modifier.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The healing rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 1st."],
"Curse Ring": ["You lay a curse on a ring you touch that nobody is wearing or carrying.",
 "You lay a curse on a ring you touch that nobody is wearing or carrying. Choose one of the effects of bestow curse when you cast this. The next creature that willingly puts on the ring suffers that effect with no saving throw. The curse passes to the wearer and the ring turns into an ordinary ring that can be removed, but the curse stays on the creature until it is removed or dispelled. Identify reveals that the ring is cursed."],
"Curse of Boreas": ["Choose a creature you can see within range.",
 "Choose a creature you can see within range. If it fails a Charisma save, it and its gear freeze into an inert statue of ice and it is effectively paralyzed. Its mind stays active and it still breathes and has a heartbeat, though both are barely noticeable. Damage or breakage done to the ice statue appears on the creature when it thaws. Dispel magic cannot end this spell, but it lets the target speak (not move or cast spells) for a number of rounds equal to the slot level used. Greater restoration or stronger magic is needed to free the creature."],
"Curse of Dust": ["You curse a creature within range that you are familiar with so that food cannot satisfy it.",
 "Casting time 10 minutes. You curse a creature within range that you are familiar with so that food cannot satisfy it. This is real and not just a feeling, since the target physically cannot draw sustenance from food. Within minutes it feels constant hunger no matter how much it eats. The target makes a Constitution save 24 hours after the casting and every 24 hours after that. On a failure it gains one level of exhaustion. The effect ends when the duration runs out or when the target succeeds on two saves in a row."],
"Curse of Hostility": ["You touch a creature, which must succeed on a Wisdom save or be cursed with the enmity of one creature type you choose: aberrations, beasts, celestials, dragons.",
 "You touch a creature, which must succeed on a Wisdom save or be cursed with the enmity of one creature type you choose: aberrations, beasts, celestials, dragons, elementals, fey, fiends, giants, humanoids, monstrosities, plants, or undead. In situations involving creatures of that type, these effects apply. Creatures of the type that are already hostile prefer to attack the target over other targets. Creatures of the type have advantage on attack rolls against the target if the target has hit that creature at least once during the encounter. The target has disadvantage on Charisma checks against creatures of the type. Remove curse ends the effect.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 4th-level slot, the duration is concentration, up to 10 minutes. With a 5th or 6th-level slot, it is 8 hours. With a 7th or 8th-level slot, it is 24 hours. With a 9th-level slot, it lasts until dispelled."],
"Curse of Incompetence": ["You make mocking gestures at a creature within range that can see you.",
 "You make mocking gestures at a creature within range that can see you. If it fails an Intelligence save, it has disadvantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma checks made to direct a battle, work out tactics, or give directions or orders to other creatures. Each time the target gives commands, directions, or orders to other creatures, those creatures roll a d4 and subtract the result from their Initiative as they struggle with the muddled orders. This covers command abilities such as the orc war chief's Battle Cry and the hobgoblin warlord's Leadership.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The maximum duration increases by 1 minute for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Curse of Yig": ["This spell turns a Small, Medium, or Large creature you can see within range into a servant of Yig.",
 "Casting time 1 minute (ritual). This spell turns a Small, Medium, or Large creature you can see within range into a servant of Yig. An unwilling creature can make a Wisdom save to negate it. A willing creature is affected automatically and stays so as long as you concentrate. The change lasts for the duration or until the target drops to 0 hit points or dies. The target's statistics, including mental ability scores, are replaced by those of a servant of Yig. Its alignment becomes neutral evil, and it is friendly to you and reverent toward the Father of Serpents. Its equipment is unchanged. An unwilling transformed creature makes a Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns. On a success the spell ends and its alignment, personality, and attitude toward you and Yig return to normal. When it returns to its normal form, it has the hit points it had before the change. If it returned because it dropped to 0 hit points, excess damage carries over to its normal form."],
"Curse of the Grave": ["You use your link to death to curse a humanoid you can see within range.",
 "You use your link to death to curse a humanoid you can see within range. It must succeed on a Constitution save or be cursed, and the pull of the grave grows stronger on its soul. Remove curse or similar magic ends it. While cursed, the target fails death saving throws on any roll except a 20. If it dies while cursed, it rises 1 round later as a vampire spawn under your control and is no longer cursed. The spawn seeks you out to serve you. You can control only one vampire spawn made by this spell, and making another turns the earlier one to dust. If you or your companions do anything harmful to the spawn, it can make a Wisdom save, and on a success it is no longer under your control."],
"Cursed Gift": ["You imbue an object with a harmful magical effect that you, or another creature touching you, is currently suffering.",
 "You imbue an object with a harmful magical effect that you, or another creature touching you, is currently suffering. If you give the object to a creature that freely accepts it while the spell lasts, the recipient makes a Charisma save. On a failure, the harmful effect is transferred to the recipient for the spell's duration or until the effect ends. Returning the object to you, destroying it, or handing it to someone else changes nothing. Remove curse and similar magic can relieve the recipient, but the harmful effect returns to the previous victim when this spell ends if the effect's own duration has not run out.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The duration increases by 24 hours for each slot level above 4th."],
"Cynophobia": ["Choose a creature you can see within range.",
 "Choose a creature you can see within range. It must succeed on a Wisdom save or gain an overwhelming fear of canids such as dogs, wolves, foxes, and worgs. For the duration, the first time the target sees a canid, it must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened of that canid until the end of its next turn. Each time it sees a different canid, it makes the save again. The target also has disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls while a canid is within 10 feet of it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 5th-level slot, the duration is 24 hours. With a 7th-level slot, it is 1 month. With an 8th or 9th-level slot, it lasts until dispelled."],
"Daggerhawk": ["Cast this on a nonmagical dagger and a ghostly hawk forms around it.",
 "Cast this on a nonmagical dagger and a ghostly hawk forms around it. The hawk and dagger fly up and make a melee attack against one creature you select within 60 feet, using your spell attack modifier. On a hit, it deals piercing damage equal to 1d4 + your Intelligence modifier. On your later turns, you can use an action to make the daggerhawk attack the same target. The daggerhawk has AC 14 and cannot be harmed, but a successful attack against it that deals bludgeoning, force, or slashing damage sends it tumbling, so it cannot attack again until after your next turn."],
"Dark Dementing": ["A shadow creeps through the target's mind and leaves behind a trace of shadow essence, causing a deep fear of the dark.",
 "A shadow creeps through the target's mind and leaves behind a trace of shadow essence, causing a deep fear of the dark. A creature you designate within range makes a Charisma save. On a failure, it is frightened of you for the duration. It can repeat the save each time it takes damage, ending the effect on a success. While frightened this way, it will not willingly enter or attack into a space that is not brightly lit. If it is in dim light or darkness, it must move toward bright light or make its own, such as by lighting a lantern or casting light."],
"Dark Heraldry": ["Dark entities announce your entry into combat and fill your enemies with dread.",
 "Dark entities announce your entry into combat and fill your enemies with dread. Choose a number of creatures up to your spellcasting ability modifier (minimum one) that you can see within range and whose alignment differs from yours. Each takes 5d8 psychic damage and is frightened of you. A creature that succeeds on a Wisdom save takes half damage and is not frightened. A creature frightened this way repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. It makes this save with disadvantage if you can see it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Dark Lord's Mantle": ["You fill yourself with fiendish power that inspires allies and cows foes.",
 "You fill yourself with fiendish power that inspires allies and cows foes. You have advantage on saving throws against enchantment spells and effects. Each ally within 30 feet of you can roll a d4 once per round and add it to an attack roll as a bonus action, or to a saving throw as a reaction. An enemy that starts its turn within 30 feet of you, or moves within 30 feet of you on its turn, must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened of you. If it leaves the area, it stays frightened until the start of its next turn, and then the spell ends for it. While frightened this way, the creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. On a success it is no longer frightened and cannot be affected by your casting of this spell again for 24 hours."],
"Dark Maw": ["Thick shadowy ichor drips from your mouth as it fills with giant shadow fangs.",
 "Thick shadowy ichor drips from your mouth as it fills with giant shadow fangs. Make a melee spell attack against the target. On a hit, it takes 1d8 necrotic damage, and if it is a humanoid you gain 1d4 temporary hit points until the start of your next turn. The damage increases by 1d8 at 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8), and 17th level (4d8). If you have a bite attack, such as from a racial trait or a spell like alter self, this spell instead adds necrotic damage equal to your spellcasting ability modifier to the bite, and you gain 1d4 temporary hit points if the target is a humanoid."],
"Dark Path": ["You conjure a shadowy road between two points within range to form a bridge or path.",
 "You conjure a shadowy road between two points within range to form a bridge or path. It can span a chasm or make a smooth way through difficult terrain. The path is 10 feet wide and up to 50 feet long, and it supports up to 500 pounds at one time. A creature that puts more weight on it than it can bear sinks through as if the path were not there."],
"Dark Web of the Spider Monarch": ["A 30-foot cube centered on you fills with sticky, night-black webbing.",
 "A 30-foot cube centered on you fills with sticky, night-black webbing. The webs are difficult terrain and lightly obscure the area. You are unaffected by those effects and gain a climbing speed of 30 feet while moving on the webs. If the webs are not anchored between two solid masses such as walls or trees, or layered across a floor, wall, or ceiling, they collapse and the spell ends at the start of your next turn. Webs layered over a flat surface are 5 feet deep. A creature that starts its turn in the webs or enters them on its turn makes a Dexterity save. On a failure, it is restrained while it stays in the webs or until it breaks free. On each of your turns that you are in the webs, you can use a bonus action to siphon life force from every creature restrained by them. Each takes 3d6 necrotic damage and you regain hit points equal to half the damage dealt. A restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC, and on a success it is no longer restrained. The webs are not flammable but are vulnerable to radiant damage. Any 5-foot cube of webs exposed to radiant damage vanishes in 1 round."],
"Darkbolt": ["You speak a quick invocation, wrap a black nimbus around your hand, and hurl three rays of darkness at one or more targets in range.",
 "You speak a quick invocation, wrap a black nimbus around your hand, and hurl three rays of darkness at one or more targets in range. You can split the rays among targets as you like. Make one ranged spell attack for each target (not each ray). Each ray that hits deals 1d10 cold damage. A target hit by one or more rays must succeed on a Constitution save or be unable to take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You create one additional ray for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Dead Walking": ["As part of the casting, you place a copper piece under your tongue.",
 "As part of the casting, you place a copper piece under your tongue. Up to six willing creatures you can see within range become invisible to undead for the duration. Anything a target wears or carries is invisible while it is on that target. The spell ends for all targets if any target attacks or casts a spell.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot, it lasts 1 hour without requiring concentration. With a 4th-level slot or higher, the duration increases by 1 hour for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Deadly Sting": ["You grow a 10-foot-long tail, supple as a whip and tipped with a horrible stinger.",
 "You grow a 10-foot-long tail, supple as a whip and tipped with a horrible stinger. As part of the casting and as an action on each of your later turns, you can make a melee spell attack with the stinger, with a reach of 10 feet. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 piercing damage plus 4d10 poison damage, and it must succeed on a Constitution save or become vulnerable to poison damage for the duration."],
"Death God's Touch": ["You can shred the life force of a creature you touch.",
 "You can shred the life force of a creature you touch. You become invisible and make a melee spell attack against the target. On a hit, it takes 10d10 necrotic damage, and if this reduces it to 0 hit points, it dies. Hit or miss, you stay invisible until the start of your next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 2d10 for each slot level above 7th."],
"Decay": ["Make a melee spell attack against a creature you touch.",
 "Make a melee spell attack against a creature you touch. On a hit, it takes 1d10 necrotic damage. If the target is a Tiny or Small nonmagical object that nobody is wearing or carrying, it automatically takes maximum damage. The damage increases by 1d10 at 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10)."],
"Decelerate": ["You slow time around a creature you can see within range.",
 "You slow time around a creature you can see within range. It must succeed on a Wisdom save or have its walking speed halved, rounded up to the nearest 5 feet. It can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Until the spell ends, on a failed save the target's speed is halved again at the start of each of your turns. For example, a creature with speed 30 that fails the first save drops to 15 feet, then to 10 feet at the start of your next turn if it fails again, then to 5 feet the round after. Decelerate cannot reduce a creature's speed below 5 feet.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can affect one additional creature for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Deep Breath": ["The recipient can breathe and function normally in thin air, suffering no ill effects at altitudes up to 20,000 feet.",
 "The recipient can breathe and function normally in thin air, suffering no ill effects at altitudes up to 20,000 feet. If you touch more than one creature during the casting, the duration is divided evenly among them.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The duration increases by 2 hours for each slot level above 1st."],
"Deep Focus": ["You draw on ambient magical energy to steady and sustain a spell.",
 "You draw on ambient magical energy to steady and sustain a spell. The next spell you cast that normally requires concentration lasts its full normal duration without needing concentration, as long as you cast it within 1 minute of casting this spell and it is 4th level or lower. This spell ends when that duration ends, or if 1 minute passes without you casting a concentration spell.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can affect any concentration spell you can cast that is one level higher than the slot used for deep focus or lower."],
"Deep Freeze": ["You blast a creature with deep cold, dealing 4d8 cold damage and encasing it in ice.",
 "You blast a creature with deep cold, dealing 4d8 cold damage and encasing it in ice. An encased creature is grappled and takes an extra 2d8 cold damage at the start of its turn each round it stays encased. If the target succeeds on a Dexterity save, it takes half damage and none of the extra damage and is not encased, but clinging ice reduces its speed by 15 feet (minimum 5 feet) until it uses an action to clear the ice. A grappled target can use an action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC, breaking free on a success. Another creature within 5 feet of the target can also make a Strength check on its turn to free it. The ice can be attacked. It has AC 12, 10 hit points, and vulnerability to fire damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 4th."],
"Defensive Quills": ["Sharp quills grow from your skin.",
 "Sharp quills grow from your skin. You can end the spell early by using an action to dismiss it. You gain a +1 bonus to AC for the duration. A creature that hits you with an attack made with a light weapon, a natural attack, or an unarmed strike takes 2d8 piercing damage from your quills. A creature that grapples you takes this damage at the start of each of its turns while grappling you. If a creature swallows you, it takes this damage each round at the start of your turn."],
"Defile Healing": ["You try to reverse the energy of the healing spell so that it deals damage instead.",
 "Reaction, taken when you see a creature cast a healing spell. You try to reverse the energy of the healing spell so that it deals damage instead. If the healing spell is cast with a slot of 5th level or lower, the slot is spent but the spell restores no hit points. Each creature targeted by the healing spell also takes necrotic damage equal to the healing it would have received, or half as much with a successful Constitution save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With an 8th-level slot, you can reverse a healing spell cast with a slot of 6th level or lower. With a 9th-level slot, you can reverse one cast with a slot of 7th level or lower."],
"Delay Potion": ["You delay the effect of the next potion you drink for up to 1 hour.",
 "You delay the effect of the next potion you drink for up to 1 hour. You must drink the potion within 1 round of casting this spell or the spell has no effect. At any point during the duration, you can use a bonus action to make the potion take effect, working as if you had just drunk it. While the potion is delayed it has no effect at all, and you can drink and benefit from other potions normally. You can delay only one potion at a time. If you try to delay a second potion, the spell fails, the first potion has no effect, and the second works normally when drunk."],
"Demon Within": ["One humanoid of your choice within range becomes a gateway for a demon to enter the plane you are on.",
 "One humanoid of your choice within range becomes a gateway for a demon to enter the plane you are on. You choose the demon's type from those of challenge rating 4 or lower. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a success, the gateway fails to open and the spell has no effect. On a failure, the target takes 4d6 force damage as the demon claws toward this world. For the duration, you can use a bonus action to agitate the demon, dealing an extra 2d6 force damage to the target each time. If the target drops to 0 hit points while affected, the demon tears out of the body and appears in the same space as its incapacitated or dead host. You do not control the demon, which may attack or leave as it chooses. It disappears after 24 hours or when it drops to 0 hit points."],
"Desiccating Breath": ["You exhale a cloud of black dust that pulls all moisture from a 30-foot cone.",
 "You exhale a cloud of black dust that pulls all moisture from a 30-foot cone. Each animal in the cone takes 4d10 necrotic damage, or half as much with a successful Constitution save. Plants and plant creatures take 6d10 instead, also halved on a successful Constitution save."],
"Desolation": ["You plant an obsidian acorn in solid ground and chant curses against the natural world for an hour.",
 "Casting time 1 hour (ritual only). You plant an obsidian acorn in solid ground and chant curses against the natural world for an hour. The land within 1 mile of the acorn then becomes infertile whatever its prior state. Nothing grows there and all plant life in the area dies over the course of a day. Plant creatures are not affected. Spells that summon plants, such as entangle, require an ability check using the caster's spellcasting ability against your spell save DC. On a success the spell works normally, and on a failure desolation counters it. After one year, the land slowly returns to normal fertility. A living creature that finishes a short rest in the area halves the result of any Hit Dice it spends. Desolation counters the effects of a bloom spell.\n\n**Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, the duration becomes permanent."],
"Destructive Resonance": ["You shout a scathing string of Void Speech that assaults the minds of those before you.",
 "You shout a scathing string of Void Speech that assaults the minds of those before you. Each creature in a 15-foot cone that can hear you takes 4d6 psychic damage, or half as much with a successful Wisdom save. A creature damaged by this spell cannot take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Detect Dragons": ["You sense dragons and other draconic creatures within your line of sight and 120 feet, regardless of disguises, illusions, and alteration magic such as polymorph.",
 "You sense dragons and other draconic creatures within your line of sight and 120 feet, regardless of disguises, illusions, and alteration magic such as polymorph. What you learn depends on how many consecutive rounds you spend an action studying a subject or area. On the first round, you learn whether any draconic creatures are present, but not their number, location, identity, or type. On the second round, you learn how many there are and the general condition of the most powerful one. On the third and later rounds, you make a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you learn the age, type, and location of one draconic creature within range. The spell gives no information on the turn you cast it unless you can take a second action that turn."],
"Detonate Corpses": ["Up to five Small or Medium corpses you can see within range explode in a hail of bone shards.",
 "Up to five Small or Medium corpses you can see within range explode in a hail of bone shards. Each creature within 20 feet of an exploding corpse takes 4d10 piercing damage, or half as much with a successful Dexterity save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 5th."],
"Deva's Wings": ["You touch a willing creature.",
 "You touch a willing creature. It grows feathery white wings that give it a flying speed of 60 feet and the ability to hover. When the target takes the Attack action, it can use a bonus action to make a melee weapon attack with the wings, with a reach of 10 feet. On a hit, the target of the attack takes bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your spellcasting ability modifier and must succeed on a Strength save or fall prone. When the spell ends, the wings vanish and the recipient falls if it is in the air.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 4th."],
"Dimensional Shove": ["You push a creature you touch through a dimensional portal so it vanishes and reappears a short distance away.",
 "You push a creature you touch through a dimensional portal so it vanishes and reappears a short distance away. If the target fails a Wisdom save, it disappears and reappears 30 feet from you in a direction you choose. It can pass through walls, creatures, or other solid surfaces on the way, but it cannot reappear inside a solid object or off solid ground. Instead it appears in the nearest safe unoccupied space along its path.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The target is shoved an additional 30 feet for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Discern Weakness": ["You divine the weak points in your foes' defenses so you can strike with deadly effect.",
 "You divine the weak points in your foes' defenses so you can strike with deadly effect. When you score a critical hit or a successful sneak attack against an opponent, roll the damage twice and take the better result."],
"Disquieting Gaze": ["Your eyes burn with shimmering motes of unholy crimson light.",
 "Your eyes burn with shimmering motes of unholy crimson light. Until the spell ends, you have advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks against creatures that can see you, and advantage on spell attack rolls that deal necrotic damage to creatures that can see your eyes."],
"Disruptive Aura": ["A warping prismatic aura surrounds and outlines each creature inside a 10-foot cube within range.",
 "A warping prismatic aura surrounds and outlines each creature inside a 10-foot cube within range. The aura sheds dim light out to 10 feet, and it outlines the locations of hidden or invisible creatures. If a creature in the area tries to cast a spell or use a magic item, it makes a Wisdom save. On a success, the spell or item works normally. On a failure, its effect is suppressed for the duration of the aura. Time spent suppressed counts against the duration of that spell or item effect.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 9th-level slot, the cube is 20 feet on a side."],
"Distracting Divination": ["Foresight tells you how to be just distracting enough to foil an enemy spellcaster.",
 "Reaction, taken when an enemy tries to cast a spell. Foresight tells you how to be just distracting enough to foil an enemy spellcaster. When an adjacent enemy tries to cast a spell, make a melee spell attack against it. On a hit, the enemy's spell fails and has no effect. The enemy's action is used up but the spell slot is not expended."],
"Distraction Cascade": ["With a flash of foresight, you throw a foe off balance.",
 "Reaction, taken when an ally declares an attack against an enemy you can see. With a flash of foresight, you throw a foe off balance. Choose one creature you can see that your ally has just declared as the target of an attack. Unless that creature succeeds on a Charisma save, attacks against it are made with advantage until the end of this turn."],
"Distressing Resonance": ["You create a field of subsonic vibrations in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you choose within range, causing physical distress and extreme discomfort.",
 "You create a field of subsonic vibrations in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you choose within range, causing physical distress and extreme discomfort. A creature in the area, or that enters it after you cast the spell, must succeed on a Constitution save or be incapacitated until the start of its next turn. On a success, it can act normally. A creature that starts its turn in the area must make the save again. Constructs, deafened creatures, oozes, plants, and undead are not affected. The vibrations interfere with tremorsense, negating its use in the area."],
"Dome of Silence": ["An invisible dome with a 10-foot radius around you dampens any sound traveling into or out of the area.",
 "An invisible dome with a 10-foot radius around you dampens any sound traveling into or out of the area. Creatures can pass through the dome normally, but sound cannot. You and creatures inside can hear each other but nothing outside, and noise made inside cannot be heard outside. Any attack that deals thunder damage dispels the dome, but the dome halves that damage to creatures inside it."],
"Doom of Blue Crystal": ["You are surrounded by a field of glowing blue energy that lasts 3 rounds.",
 "You are surrounded by a field of glowing blue energy that lasts 3 rounds. Creatures within 5 feet of you, including you, make a Constitution save when the spell is cast and again at the start of each of your turns while it lasts. A creature that fails is restrained. A restrained creature that fails is paralyzed. A paralyzed creature that fails is petrified and becomes a statue of blue crystal. As with any concentration spell, you can end the field at any time with no action. If you are turned to crystal, the spell ends after all affected creatures make their saves. Restrained and paralyzed creatures recover immediately when the spell ends, but petrification is permanent. Creatures turned to crystal can see, hear, and smell normally, and do not need to eat or breathe. If shatter is cast on a crystal creature, it must succeed on a Constitution save against the caster's spell save DC or be killed. Creatures turned to blue crystal can be restored with dispel magic, greater restoration, or comparable magic."],
"Doom of Consuming Fire": ["You are wreathed in cold purple fire that harms creatures near you.",
 "You are wreathed in cold purple fire that harms creatures near you. You take 1d6 cold damage each round for the duration. Creatures within 5 feet of you when you cast the spell, and at the start of each of your turns while it lasts, take 1d8 cold damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot, the fire extends 10 feet from you, you take 1d8 cold damage, and other creatures take 1d10 cold damage. With a 4th-level slot, it extends 15 feet, you take 1d10, and others take 1d12. With a slot of 5th level or higher, it extends 20 feet, you take 1d12, and others take 1d20."],
"Doom of Dancing Blades": ["You create 1d4 illusory copies of a weapon of your choice that float in the air 5 feet from you.",
 "You create 1d4 illusory copies of a weapon of your choice that float in the air 5 feet from you. They move with you, spinning, shifting, and mimicking your attacks. When a melee attack hits you but the attack roll beat your AC by 3 or less, an illusory weapon parries it. You take no damage and the illusory weapon is destroyed. When a melee attack hits you and the illusory weapons cannot parry it (the roll beat your AC by 4 or more), you take half damage and an illusory weapon is destroyed. Spells and effects that affect an area or need no attack roll affect you normally and do not destroy any illusory weapons. If you score a critical hit with a melee attack while this spell is on you, all your illusory weapons also strike the target, each dealing 1d8 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage (your choice). The spell ends when the duration expires or all the illusory weapons are destroyed or used up. An attacker must be able to see the illusory weapons to be affected. The spell has no effect if you are invisible or in total darkness, or if the attacker is blinded."],
"Doom of Disenchantment": ["Your worn armor and clothing glow with light.",
 "Your worn armor and clothing glow with light. When a creature hits you with an attack, the spell counters any magic that gives the attack a bonus to hit or to damage. For example, a +1 weapon is still magical but gets neither +1 to hit nor +1 to damage against you. The spell also suppresses other magical properties of the attack. A sword of wounding cannot cause ongoing wounds on you, and you recover hit points lost to its damage normally. If the attack was a spell, it is affected as if you had cast counterspell, using Charisma as your spellcasting ability. Spells with an instantaneous duration are unaffected."],
"Doom of Serpent Coils": ["You drink a dose of venom or other poison and spread its effect to other living things around you.",
 "You drink a dose of venom or other poison and spread its effect to other living things around you. If the poison normally allows a saving throw, your save automatically fails. You suffer the poison's effect normally before spreading it to all other living creatures within 10 feet of you. Instead of the usual save against the poison, each creature around you makes a Constitution save against this spell. On a success, a target suffers no damage or other effect from the poison and is immune to further castings of doom of serpent coils for 24 hours. On a failure, a target does not suffer the poison's usual effect and instead takes 4d6 poison damage and is poisoned. While poisoned this way, a creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. On a failure, it takes 4d6 poison damage again and stays poisoned. On a success, it is no longer poisoned and is immune to further castings for 24 hours. Multiple castings have no added effect on creatures already poisoned by it. Protection from poison or comparable magic can end the effect."],
"Doom of the Cracked Shield": ["Cast this on a melee weapon.",
 "Cast this on a melee weapon. The next time the weapon is used, it destroys the target's nonmagical shield or damages its nonmagical armor, in addition to the normal effect of the attack. A nonmagical shield breaks into pieces. If the foe has no shield, its nonmagical armor takes a -2 penalty to AC. If the target uses neither armor nor a shield, the spell is spent with no effect."],
"Doom of the Earthen Maw": ["The ground within 30 feet of a point you choose turns into filthy, slippery muck.",
 "The ground within 30 feet of a point you choose turns into filthy, slippery muck. The spell affects sand, earth, mud, and ice but not stone, wood, or other material. For the duration, the ground in the area is difficult terrain. A creature in the area when you cast the spell must succeed on a Strength save or be restrained by the mud until the spell ends. A restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength save and free itself. A creature that frees itself, or that enters the area after the casting, is slowed by the difficult terrain but is not restrained. Each round, a restrained creature sinks deeper. A Medium or smaller creature restrained for 3 rounds is submerged at the end of its third turn, and a Large creature is submerged after 4 rounds. Submerged creatures begin suffocating if they are not holding their breath. A creature still submerged when the spell ends is sealed beneath the newly hardened ground. It can escape only if someone digs it out or it has a burrowing speed."],
"Doom of the Pit": ["You create a ripple of dark energy that destroys everything it touches.",
 "You create a ripple of dark energy that destroys everything it touches. A cylindrical extradimensional hole, 10 feet in radius and 10 feet deep, appears on a horizontal surface of sufficient size. It extends into another dimension, so it has no weight and does not displace the material beneath it. You can make it in a ship's deck as easily as in a dungeon floor or forest ground. The pit's radius grows by 10 feet at the start of your turn each round. A creature standing in the original space, or in a space the pit grows into, must succeed on a Dexterity save or fall in. A creature adjacent to the pit when it grows must also succeed on a Dexterity save or fall in. Creatures subjected to a successful pushing effect, such as gust of wind, do not make this save. Creatures that fall in take normal falling damage. The walls are slick and slimy and need a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check to climb. Creatures and objects in the pit take 1d6 necrotic damage at the start of each of their turns. If you fall into your own pit, you take damage, the spell ends, and you are incapacitated for 2 rounds. When the spell ends, the pit floor rises and carries creatures back to the original surface. Each creature in the pit then makes a Constitution save. On a failure, it is stunned for 2 rounds after the spell ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The pit's depth increases by 10 feet for each slot level above 4th."],
"Doom of the Slippery Rogue": ["This spell covers a 20-foot by 20-foot section of wall or floor within range with a thin coat of grease.",
 "This spell covers a 20-foot by 20-foot section of wall or floor within range with a thin coat of grease. Each climber on an affected vertical surface must succeed on a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check or fall at once, unless held in place by ropes or other climbing gear. A creature standing on an affected floor falls prone unless it succeeds on a Dexterity save. Creatures that try to climb or move through the area move at no more than half speed (cumulative with the usual reduction for climbing), and each movement must be followed by a Strength save (climbing) or Dexterity save (walking). On a failed save, the creature falls or falls prone."],
"Douse Light": ["With a simple gesture, you put out one small source of light within range.",
 "With a simple gesture, you put out one small source of light within range. This extinguishes a torch, a candle, a lantern, or a light or dancing lights cantrip."],
"Draconic Majesty": ["You exude the presence of a dragon.",
 "You exude the presence of a dragon. All creatures within 30 feet of you that are aware of you must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The radius increases by 30 feet for each slot level above 3rd, to a maximum of 120 feet with a slot of 6th level or higher."],
"Draconic Senses": ["You sharpen your senses to those of a dragon.",
 "You sharpen your senses to those of a dragon. For the duration, you gain darkvision out to 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, its range increases by 60 feet. You also gain blindsight out to 60 feet."],
"Draconic Smite": ["The next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during the duration, your weapon takes the form of a silver dragon's head.",
 "The next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during the duration, your weapon takes the form of a silver dragon's head. The attack deals an extra 1d6 cold damage, and up to four other creatures of your choice within 30 feet of the target must each succeed on a Constitution save or take 1d6 cold damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The extra cold damage, and the cold damage to the other creatures, increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 1st."],
"Dragon Breath": ["You summon draconic power and gain a breath weapon.",
 "You summon draconic power and gain a breath weapon. When you cast the spell, you can immediately exhale a 15-foot cone or a 30-foot line of elemental energy, depending on the dragon type you choose. While the spell lasts, roll a d6 at the start of each of your turns. On a 5 or 6, you can use a bonus action that turn to use the breath weapon again. Your choice of dragon type sets the area and damage of the breath for the duration. Black: 30-foot line, 5 feet wide, 6d6 acid damage. Blue: 30-foot line, 5 feet wide, 6d6 lightning damage. Green: 15-foot cone, 6d6 poison damage. Red: 15-foot cone, 6d6 fire damage. White: 15-foot cone, 6d6 cold damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 2d6 for each slot level above 5th."],
"Dragon Roar": ["Your amplified voice assaults the mind of one creature.",
 "Your amplified voice assaults the mind of one creature. The target makes a Charisma save. On a failure, it takes 1d4 psychic damage and is frightened until the start of your next turn. A target can be affected by your dragon roar only once per 24 hours. The damage increases by 1d4 at 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4), and 17th level (4d4)."],
"Dragon's Pride": ["Your sense of self swells to draconic proportions.",
 "Your sense of self swells to draconic proportions. Until the spell ends, you have advantage on all Charisma checks and on saving throws against being charmed or frightened."],
"Drain Item": ["You touch a magic item and drain its magical energy.",
 "You touch a magic item and drain its magical energy. If another creature carries or holds the item, you must hit the wielder's AC with a melee spell attack to touch it. On a hit, the item loses 1d3 charges. If this brings the item to 0 charges, any effects that happen when it runs out of charges take place immediately.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You drain more charges: 1d4 with a 5th-level slot, 1d6 with a 6th-level slot, 1d8 with a 7th-level slot, or 2d6 with an 8th or 9th-level slot."],
"Dread Wings": ["A swarm of flying, bat-like shapes forms in a 20-foot-radius cloud around the point you target.",
 "A swarm of flying, bat-like shapes forms in a 20-foot-radius cloud around the point you target. A creature that starts its turn in the swarm takes 4d8 necrotic damage and must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened for 1d4 rounds. Creatures immune to necrotic damage cannot be frightened by it. You can use an action on your turn to move the swarm up to 40 feet in any direction."],
"Drown": ["You fill a creature's lungs with seawater.",
 "You fill a creature's lungs with seawater. Unless the target succeeds on a Constitution save, it begins suffocating at once. A suffocating creature cannot speak or perform verbal spell components. It can hold its breath and then survive a number of rounds equal to its Constitution modifier (minimum 1 round), after which it drops to 0 hit points and is dying. Huge or larger creatures are unaffected, as are creatures that can breathe water or do not need air. A creature that is suffocating (not dying) can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Dryad's Kiss": ["You perform an ancient incantation that summons flora from the fey realm.",
 "You perform an ancient incantation that summons flora from the fey realm. A creature you can see within range is covered in small purple buds and takes 3d8 necrotic damage. A successful Wisdom save negates the damage but not the plant growth. The target, or an ally of the target within 5 feet, can remove the buds by using an action to succeed on an Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Medicine) check against your spell save DC. Greater restoration or blight also removes them. While the buds remain, whenever the target takes damage from a source other than this spell, one bud blossoms into a purple and yellow flower that deals an extra 1d8 necrotic damage to the target. Once four blossoms have formed, the buds can no longer be removed by nonmagical means. The buds and blossoms wilt and fall away when the spell ends, provided the creature is still alive. If an affected creature dies, sweet-smelling blossoms quickly cover its body and wilt after one month.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a slot of 5th level or higher, the number of targets increases by one for every two slot levels above 3rd."],
"Dying of the Light": ["A wave of withering darkness erupts from you and fills a 120-foot-radius sphere, putting out all nonmagical light sources in the area.",
 "A wave of withering darkness erupts from you and fills a 120-foot-radius sphere, putting out all nonmagical light sources in the area. Light from spells of 6th level or lower is dispelled. Magic items (not artifacts) that give off light have that property suppressed while in the area. Light sources brought into the area during the duration are also extinguished. Only light-producing spells of 7th level or higher work inside. Nonmagical light sources taken out of the area can be relit, and magic items regain their light 1 round after leaving. This magical darkness defeats darkvision, except for creatures that can see in magical darkness, such as devils. You can see within the area as if it were brightly lit. Each creature you choose that ends its turn in the darkness takes 4d8 necrotic damage and gains one level of exhaustion. A successful Constitution save halves the damage and negates the exhaustion."],
}
